@@ -7,6 +7,11 @@ VHF band (AM, 108-137 MHz) and FM broadcast (65-108 MHz), and how RadioFoundry d
 Both are receive only and need no menu: the frequency decides. An FM channel or the VFO in the air band is received
 in AM; one in the broadcast band plays on the broadcast receiver.
 
+A board can designate an active RX-only frequency band for fixed 12.5 kHz FM. The VFO and stored channels use
+the channel receiver there, with ordinary FM squelch and RX sub-audio. This profile takes precedence over AM or
+digital channel tags and over the broadcast tuner. PTT is refused if either side of a channel is in the band.
+The on-radio channel editor saves this profile as narrow FM, RX only.
+
 ## 1. Which radios
 
 A radio has air band receive when its build has `CONFIG_AM_RX` and its board sets `CAP_AM_RX` and `rx_am`, and
